From 26a6b2e6e0647d43d192f04a8835cf821ff772cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0226: Replayable Quest Chains -- resolution logic and
 purchasing

Step (3) of the sequencing plan. Wires the data model (0224) and loot
mechanism (0225) into something a hero can actually be sent on. Still
no dedicated UI -- callable, not yet reachable from the interface.

QuestManager.chainReplayOffer: replay counterpart to chainOffer, with
the chosen difficulty's successPenalty/durationMultiplier baked into
baseSuccess/duration at generation time -- consistent with how
ordinary quest/chain offers already lock success in at commit via
previewSuccess, unlike raids which apply the penalty fresh at resolve.
Distinct id namespace (chainReplay: vs chain:).

New fields, not overloading existing ones: QuestOffer.chain.replay,
QuestResult.chainReplayAdvanced (existing chainAdvanced-reading UI
code assumes activeChains/completedChains correspondence, which a
replay never touches).

QuestManager.resolve's chain section now branches three ways:
ordinary quest (untouched), first-clear chain stage (untouched), or
replay (new). Replay branch: padding loot tagged
chainReplayHeroic/chainReplayLegendary (Normal falls through
unchanged); dedicated item chance roll on a completed final stage
(baseDropChance + difficulty's lootBonus, never at Normal); full
attempt reset to stage 0 on failure (not a same-stage retry, confirmed
design); never touches ChainDef's own first-clear-only rewards.

GuildManager.buyChainReplayTier: flat one-time gold, no levels.

Two new engine actions: startChainReplay(heroId, chainId, difficulty)
-- checks isChainReplayEligible, builds the offer, sends through the
same QuestManager.start every quest uses, no Auto-Chain interaction
(same reasoning pickBestQuest already excludes chain offers
entirely). buyChainReplayTier(tierId) -- thin wrapper.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean against
the final re-based tree. Every new Tuning.get() call cross-checked by
script against registered ids -- 17/17 match exactly. No duplicate
Tuning ids introduced. SAVE_VERSION correctly untouched (no new
persisted fields this step).
